<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sherbro Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sherbro Island is an island off the southern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a>. In 1820 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-colonization-society">American Colonization Society</a> landed its first settlers of free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-americans">African Americans</a> there, but disease killed many of them, and the survivors moved in 1821–1822 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-mesurado">Cape Mesurado</a>, where the colony that became Liberia was founded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sherbro-island.jpg" alt="Sherbro Island" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sherbro_Landsat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
